🧪 Contract Testing – Demo Notes & Feedback
✅ Overall Feedback
Great job so far — strong foundational work and clear understanding of API testing objectives.

Team has successfully implemented initial contract testing setup and mock validation.

The use of Pact is appropriate and aligns well with microservice-based architecture principles.

⚠️ Key Gaps & Action Items
🚫 No CI/CD Integration Yet

Currently, tests are not automatically triggered or validated as part of CI/CD pipelines.

📌 Action: Integrate contract tests into GitHub Actions/Jenkins pipelines for automated verification during PRs and builds.

📉 No Comprehensive Reporting

Lack of structured, accessible reporting (e.g., failed contract cases, verification coverage).

📌 Action: Output test results in JUnit/JSON format and push to a central reporting dashboard or qTest.

🧩 Missing Test Management Integration

Tests not linked to user stories, requirements, or acceptance criteria.

📌 Action: Connect test results to qTest to ensure traceability and visibility in QA lifecycle.

🧼 No Static Validation Process (Linting)

No enforcement of API design best practices or standards.

📌 Action: Introduce Spectral (OpenAPI linter) in pre-commit hooks or CI to validate OpenAPI specs against company standards.

🧾 Pact Framework Setup Needs Maturity

Pact is used, but contracts are not versioned, published, or brokered across services.

📌 Action: Implement Pact Broker for centralized contract sharing and version control.

🔄 No Formal Consumer-Driven Workflow

No clear process to drive contract definition from the consumer side and verify it on provider side.

📌 Action: Define a consumer-driven contract testing workflow, with:

Pact files generated by consumers.

Published to Pact Broker.

Verified by providers in CI.

